@meeting endFirstMorning
// The first morning of the endgame (E-4, EN2 for lead 39; plans/ending-spec.html, "If you stay"): Monday Day 36 at
// breakfast in the mess, the morning after the crossing back. The Captain sits down at your table (her own breakfast,
// else 07:30; section 29c's OCCASIONS.endFirstMorning, a chance meeting like Vance's bridge invite). A stand-in for
// SW6's words (about 10 lines). They/them for you, or your name. The Admiral is her fish.
title: Breakfast with the Captain
from: Captain Odile Marrow
gist: The Captain looked for you at breakfast: the Wren is back on her course, and she's glad you stayed.
== lines
marrow > you: Is this seat taken? It is now.   [gesture]
marrow: Back on our own side of the Line. Course laid in, nothing on the long-range. A quiet week, Vance promises.
marrow: He promises that every week.
marrow > you: I wrote to headquarters last night. Told them you're spoken for.
? choice
* Thank you, Captain.   rel:marrow+1
  marrow: Don't. It was the easiest letter I've written all year.
* What happens now?   rel:marrow+1
  marrow: Now? Breakfast. Then the board, then dinner. Then tomorrow. That's the whole secret of a ship.
* (Raise your mug)   rel:marrow+2
  marrow: To the Wren. And to the people who stay with her.
marrow: The Admiral sends his regards. I'm told.
marrow > you: Eat up. The ship's not going anywhere without you. Not any more.   [nod]
